{"page_id": "tables_derived-PMC2180171.1_doc-p5", "markdown": "# BMC Psychiatry 2007, 7:64\n\nhttp://www.biomedcentral.com/1471-244X/7/64\n\nTable 3: Sociodemographic and clinical characteristics of cases of suicide attempters in the high and low lethality group\n\nHigh lethality group (N = 225) Low lethality group (N = 95)\n\nN (S)\n\nN (%)\n\nAnalysis\n\nGender\n\nAge\n\nStay in hospical (days)\n\nMarital stasus\n\nMale Female\n\nMale middle age\n\nMeans\n\nMeant\n\nSingle Married Divorced Widowed\n\nCommon-law\n\nEmployed status\n\nCurrent psychiatric treatment\n\nEmployed\n\nUnemplayed\n\nLiving status\n\nOutpatient\n\nHospitalization\n\nNo creatment\n\nAlane\n\nTogether\n\nRecent stressful life evens\n\n>2\n\nEducation\n\nCompulsory education\n\nHim school eduelton ana aver\n\nPrevious deliberate self harm\n\n>2\n\nPrevious suicide attemps\n\nFamily history of suicide/attempt\n\nAxis 1\n\nMood disorders\n\nHo ustment dorders\n\nSchizophrenia and other psychotic disorders\n\nSubstance-related disorders\n\n> 2\n\nPersonality disorders\n\n§Mann-Whitney U test\n\n96 (43)\n\n129 (57)\n\n34 (15)\n\n39.8土15.7\n\n23.0土41.3\n\n87 (39)\n\nBI (36)\n\n31 (14)\n\n2 (I)\n\n14 (6)\n\n95(42)\n\n126 (56)\n\n135 (60)\n\n4(2)\n\n71 (32)\n\n51 (23)\n\n172(76)\n\n73 (32)\n\n80 (36)\n\n47 (21)\n\n53 (24)\n\n150 (67)\n\n145 (64)\n\n18 (8)\n\nSO (22)\n\n121(54)\n\n51 (23)\n\n38（17）\n\n34 (15)\n\n58 (26)\n\n33 (15)\n\n43（19）\n\n29 (13)\n\n71 (32)\n\nF60-69 had also decreased. The present study is the first large-scale study involving a comprehensive evaluation of attempted suicide cases in Japan since the dramatic increase in the suicide rate began.\n\n30 (32)\n\n65 (68)\n\n9 (9)\n\n34.8= 15.9\n\n5.0+4.1\n\n41 (16)\n\n27 (28)\n\n7 (7)\n\n1(1)\n\n7 (7)\n\n38 (40)\n\n52 (55)\n\n69 (73)\n\n0 (0)\n\n18 (19)\n\n(17% (18\n\n73 (77)\n\n22 (23)\n\n42 (14)\n\n20(21)\n\n25 (26)\n\n57 (60)\n\n39 (41)\n\n70\n\n40 (42)\n\n47 (49)\n\n16(17)\n\n25 (26)\n\n10(11)\n\n20(21)\n\n24 (25)\n\n11 (12)\n\n7 (7)\n\n39(41)\n\n5.9\n\n2=-8.7\n\n6.6\n\nก.ร.\n\n0.05 >\n\n0.01 >\n\n＜0.001\n\nก.ร.\n\nn.s.\n\nn.ร.\n\n<0.05\n\nn.s.\n\nn.s.\n\nก.ร.\n\nns.\n\nก.ร.\n\nn.s.\n\nThe most common method of attempted suicide in our subjects was self-poisoning, and the majority of patients who overdosed used psychotropic drugs that had been prescribed. It is known that methods vary between countries and regions. Jumping from a high place seemed more common in our subjects than in previous studies [17-19].\n\nOur center is located in an urban area containing many high-rise office buildings. Therefore, it is possible that there was a selection bias. Conversely, ingestion of pesticides or agricultural chemicals was very rare in our urban population. Attempts using firearms were also rare. Pos-\n\nPage 5 of 7\n\n(page number not for citation purposes)", "width": 1695, "height": 2200, "blocks": [{"kind": "heading", "text": "BMC Psychiatry 2007, 7:64", "bbox": {"x": 142.01351327741168, "y": 109.99999996826921, "width": 316.0945945945946, "height": 41.2500000000001}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "http://www.biomedcentral.com/1471-244X/7/64", "bbox": {"x": 1012.4189186898647, "y": 114.58333331938411, "width": 526.8243243243243, "height": 32.08333333333322}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Table 3: Sociodemographic and clinical characteristics of cases of suicide attempters in the high and low lethality group", "bbox": {"x": 146.59459003113312, "y": 233.7499998766026, "width": 1241.4729729729727, "height": 32.08333333333322}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "High lethality group (N = 225) Low lethality group (N = 95)", "bbox": {"x": 778.7837833215854, "y": 284.16666663802084, "width": 526.8243243243243, "height": 32.08333333333322}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "N (S)", "bbox": {"x": 879.567567491216, "y": 311.66666639930565, "width": 64.13513513513523, "height": 32.08333333333322}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "N (%)", "bbox": {"x": 1154.4324322033783, "y": 316.24999991185894, "width": 59.55405405405401, "height": 22